    <bpmn:process id="W_W3479" name="W3479. Remodel Site Survey, Permitting &amp; Regulatory Compliance" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Scope/design (W3475/W3477); pre-construction
Frequency: Per remodel
Volume: ~30–40 remodels/year
Owner: Real Estate / Compliance
Participants: Real Estate, Compliance/Regulatory (links to VS-22), LGU Specialist (links to VS-76), Facilities (links to VS-20.3), Store Manager, Contractor
Source: workflow W3479 — Remodel Site Survey, Permitting &amp; Regulatory Compliance</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W3479_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W3479_Lane1" name="Real Estate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3479_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3479_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3479_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W3479_Lane2" name="Compliance">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3479_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3479_End8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W3479_Start4" name="Scope/design (W3475/W3477); pre-construction">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3479_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3479_Task5" name="Real Estate/Contractor conduct the pre-construction site survey: as-built…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Real Estate/Contractor conduct the pre-construction site survey: as-built verification, structural/MEP condition, hazardous-material survey (lead/asbestos in older stores links to VS-24.3), utility capacity, and constraints (tenant/leaseholder consent where BuildRight is lessee links to VS-42; landlord notice links to VS-97)
Responsible (R): Real Estate / Contractor / Facilities
Accountable (A): VP Store Operations
Duration: Per remodel</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3479_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3479_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3479_Task6" name="Compliance/LGU Specialist secure the required permits: building/alteration…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Compliance/LGU Specialist secure the required permits: building/alteration permit, electrical/plumbing/sanitary permits, fire-safety (BFP links to VS-22), LGU permits per region (links to VS-76), and DENR where hazmat/abatement is needed (links to VS-24.3/VS-73); manage inspections and approvals
Responsible (R): Compliance / LGU Specialist
Accountable (A): VP Store Operations
Duration: Per remodel</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3479_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3479_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3479_Task7" name="Real Estate/Compliance confirm permit completeness, insurance/risk (links to…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Real Estate/Compliance confirm permit completeness, insurance/risk (links to VS-26) and HSE plan (links to VS-24), notify the landlord/LGU and neighbors of works, and release construction to start (W3483); maintain the permit/inspection record for audit (links to VS-88)
Responsible (R): Real Estate / Compliance
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: Per remodel</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3479_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3479_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W3479_End8" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W3479_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W3479_Annotation9">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-136 (ensure remodel capex &amp; handover control.) | - operational: early application and LGU relationship (links to VS-76); operational: hazmat survey and abatement plan (links to VS-24)
Owner: Real Estate / Compliance</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
